{"meta":{"id":"dm.aHR0cDovL3NlcnZlcjEuZGhha2Ftb3ZpZS5jb20vTW92aWVzL0hvbGx5d29vZC8xOTk5LS1CZWZvcmUvSmlubmFoJTIwJTI4MTk5OCUyOS8","type":"movie","name":"Jinnah","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342/6gNDyfZhQEOkeVWbsfTMOuvXx8V.jpg","background":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/vnQhzxHqAeZK5mkevV0yl9QYxiZ.jpg","description":"Biography of Mohammed Ali Jinnah, the founder of modern Pakistan is told through flashbacks as his soul tries to find eternal rest. The flashbacks start in 1947 as Jinnah pleads for a separate nation for the Muslim minority, infuriating Lord Mountbatten. Mountbatten then tries to enlist Gandhi & Nehru to persuade Jinnah to stop his efforts. Gandhi sides with Jinnah, which upsets Nehru. However, Jinnah turns down the offer to become prime minister and the film takes another slide back to 1916, which reveals all of the political implications that have occurred.\n\nRated U · Released 7 Nov 1998 · Pakistan · Language: Urdu · 110 min\nStudio: Dehlavi Films, The Quaid Project, Petra Film\n\nOn your server — Audio: Urdu","releaseInfo":"1998","genres":["History","War","Drama","Hollywood"],"imdbRating":"6.9","runtime":"110 min","cast":["Christopher Lee","James Fox","Maria Aitken","Shashi Kapoor","Richard Lintern","Indira Varma","Sam Dastor","Robert Ashby"],"director":["Jamil Dehlavi"],"released":"1998-11-07T00:00:00.000Z","slogan":"He fought for justice, and made Pakistan.","app_extras":{"cast":[{"name":"Jamil Dehlavi","character":"Director","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/v8U5x9n7nHsyL1GKt5eT9q7H4wx.jpg"},{"name":"Christopher Lee","character":"Muhammad Ali Jinnah","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/dA26fBr3t7mKqjn3OYW6kbD1LXM.jpg"},{"name":"James Fox","character":"Mountbatten","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/fO11c8zUNNgNhYu4aLxgYiBoo6R.jpg"},{"name":"Maria Aitken","character":"Edwina","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/68hYz23dvcanehgrkgEis3yn0L7.jpg"},{"name":"Shashi Kapoor","character":"Narrator","photo":"https://image.tm